================================================================================
DISCOVERED ISSUES
================================================================================

1. TEST FIXTURES INCOMPATIBLE WITH STORAGE CODE
   - JsonStorage expects nested format: boards -> columns -> tasks
   - Original conftest.py used flat format: separate boards/columns/tasks arrays
   - Root cause: _dict_to_kanban() iterates nested format first, flat format
     code never reached
   - Resolution: Updated fixtures to use nested format

2. COMMENTED-OUT ENDPOINTS NOT TESTED
   - POST /api/boards
   - PUT /api/boards/{id}
   - DELETE /api/boards/{id}
   - POST /api/columns
   - PUT /api/columns/{id}
   - DELETE /api/columns/{id}
   - DELETE /api/tasks/{id}
   - GET /api/tasks/{id}
   - GET /api/boards/{id}/columns
   - GET /api/tasks/{id}
   These were intentionally left untested per requirements

3. JSON BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY BROKEN
   - JsonStorage._dict_to_kanban() has code for flat format but it never runs
   - The nested format loop executes first and fails on flat data
   - Production kanban.json uses nested format, so this is not a production issue
   - But test fixtures with flat format will fail

